homelab-ai (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * An upstream error whose body is a plain string (or no JSON at all) is
    recorded as such instead of failing the request handler.

 -- Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>  Fri, 14 Nov 2026 16:00:00 -0600

homelab-ai (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * postinst: the config values were handed to perl as trailing arguments
    (read as file names), so every substitution came out empty and the
    service never listened. They now go in through the environment, and a
    config with empty values is refused rather than written.

 -- Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>  Fri, 14 Nov 2026 14:20:00 -0600

homelab-ai (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release (post-cutover #76): the one Anthropic client in the fleet.
    POST /internal/v1/ai/messages with a client token passes a Messages API
    request through byte for byte with the key added and the API version
    pinned; every call is recorded in ai.requests (client, consent, model,
    tokens, cache reads, latency, status); a per-client daily request budget
    answers 429 before money is spent; GET /internal/v1/ai/usage totals it.
    One container to start (not critical: callers degrade to their non-AI
    paths when it is down), built like every pool app so more can follow.

 -- Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>  Fri, 14 Nov 2026 13:30:00 -0600
